# The harness input and output. Its code lives in src/overlayr/eval/ and stays
# in the repository; these three are the data it reads and the files it writes,
# and none of them belong to anyone but this machine:
#
#   TestingImage/   24 captures plus _Answer.txt ground truth, ~20MB of other
#                   people's comics and documents
#   eval_data/      the dataset layout the harness also accepts (still empty)
#   eval_results/   run output - JSON scores plus ~13MB of rendered frames
#
# Losing the JSON means a fresh clone cannot diff against an earlier run. The
# numbers that decisions were actually made on are written into CLAUDE.md
# instead, which is where they need to survive.
TestingImage/
eval_data/
eval_results/

# Claude Code local files
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
